    "findings": [
      "MemoryValidator uses safe-integer checks, positive alignment and subtraction-based bounds checking; custom alignment need not be a power of two. Zero-length access at capacity passes.",
      "StaticMemoryPool.computeRatio is not range/finite validated. Allocation rounds fractional requests upward and zero bytes consumes one block. The fixed backing buffer is bounded, but free-lists, Maps, Sets and returned handles allocate dynamically; search/sort cost depends on pool state. Flight lock blocks allocation but not freeing or existing-memory writes.",
      "assertLive checks only pointer and generation, then i32/u8 trust caller-supplied Block.bytes. Block size/segment and pool ownership are not authenticated. free(ptr) accepts no generation, so stale pointer possession is not distinguished from the current allocation.",
      "SegmentationController.assertAccess checks one pointer segment, not the accessed range, allocation lifetime or permission for the exposed writable buffer. TypeScript private fields are not JavaScript private custody.",
      "TPLStateBuffer caches an Int32Array view and does not recheck allocation generation after construction; views survive free/reallocation. It allocates from compute, whose free fill is 0xff and therefore decodes as corruption. Index guards omit integer/NaN checks; loadTrits can partially mutate before a later invalid value/index throws.",
      "LocalSramBus reads return copies, but bounds are checked against the whole pool rather than channel-local capacity. Negative channel-relative offsets can pass when the resulting global address is valid. Bus access has no segmentation/liveness check; external photonic attachment is refused and local integrity is a constant true.",
      "Existing Fungi assets cover stride, bounded validation, allocation/policy, segmentation and trit decisions only. memory-validator.fungi::alignUp lacks TypeScript invalid-input/MAX_SAFE_INTEGER guards, and scrubFillByte returns zero for unknown segments while TypeScript frees every non-governance segment with 0xff; equivalence requires the exact admitted segment union."
